From 313b43eb2d7b217fbea1829db54f08ba43f71995 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: revvv991 <345025393+revvv991@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] turnip/kgsl: recover from an invalidated KGSL context
 (TU_KGSL_RECOVER)

After more than 3 GPU faults within 2 s KGSL invalidates the context and
every later submission fails with EDEADLK, which Turnip reported as a
lost device. The A735 CP (Retroid Pocket G2) faults in such bursts now and
then. The queue now moves to a new KGSL context and resubmits there: only
the work KGSL dropped is lost. Timestamps of the old context count as
signaled (waits, semaphore merges, sync file export); a guilty reset
status moves the queue on its next submission. TU_KGSL_RECOVER=0 keeps
the lost device.

Also fixes kgsl_syncobj_merge, which merged the -1 fd of a timestamp
syncobj when it met a sync file or a timestamp of another queue.

TU_KGSL_FAULT_TEST=<s>[i] injects a fault burst <s> seconds after the
first submission (separate IBs of zeros, or with i before the IBs of the
next four submissions) to exercise the recovery.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
